    },
    {
      "id": "e348",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2300,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 552.75,
      "height": 1050.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1676093469,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 664803083,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1  Stats stay visible at all times: lives, gold, level, score,\n   turn (WEB-03). Both screens add the stored high score,\n   raised by games and runs (WEB-18). Lives turn red at 1.\n2  Quest board: ads keep the game's order. The player can sort\n   by reward, expiry or risk. No bot pick, no EV by default (FUN-01).\n   Risk badges are colored and labeled, so color is never the\n   only signal (NFR-03). Encrypted ads appear decoded, with a tag.\n3  Every quest has the same Solve button. Risk shows through the\n   label and 'At stake: 1 life'. Trap tags only appear with the\n   advisor on (WEB-07).\n4  Shop: items the user can't afford are disabled, with a tooltip\n   showing the missing gold (WEB-04).\n   Potion first, because it's the most common purchase.\n5  Event log: newest first. Green = success, red = failure or\n   lost life, blue = purchase (WEB-05).\n6  Run form: validated inline (VAL-04). Stop is enabled only\n   while the selected run is running (WEB-08, BOT-12).\n7  Run list: status badges (running / finished / stopped /\n   failed). Clicking a run opens its live view and history.\n8  Score chart: a dashed 1000 target line shows progress toward\n   the goal at a glance (WEB-09).\n9  Live events stream over SSE with a 'live' dot. The log\n   auto-scrolls unless the user has scrolled up.\n10 Mobile: one column, with stats in a 3x2 grid. Shop, reputation and\n   log open as bottom sheets, with a bottom tab bar for navigation (NFR-01).\n11 Choose: Solve sends the API call at once and locks the other Solve\n   buttons (status: resolving). Shop, Refresh and Investigate stay\n   enabled and queue (WEB-12). Nothing is chosen for the player.\n12 Suspense, in a dialog over the board: the stakes\n   (win gold / lose a life), the risk label and an animation. Hold the result for a minimum time\n   even if the API answers first (FUN-02, FUN-03).\n13 Climax: the copy changes, the progress bar fills, and tension\n   grows with risk (FUN-05).\n14 Reveal, in the same dialog after the suspense phase.\n   Clearly different success and failure, with the game's message\n   and deltas. The stats animate. The result stays until the player\n   presses Continue or Close, then the board is back (FUN-04). Failure on the last\n   life suggests a potion.\n15 Advisor (opt-in): EV and trap tags, but never reorders the\n   board or marks a best pick (WEB-07). EV = p x reward -\n   (1 - p) x lifeCost, lifeCost = 240 / lives (CORE-06).\n   Calculation shown below the advisor sketch.\n16 Milestones: 1000 points, new high score, last life (FUN-08).\n17 Reputation: people, state and underworld, shown with a sign.\n   Unknown until the player presses Investigate, which uses one\n   turn, so it is never automatic. A new game clears it (WEB-16).\n\nResponsive breakpoints\n- < 640px: one column, bottom tabs, sheets\n- 640-1023px: ad grid with 2 columns; shop, reputation and log below\n- >= 1024px: ads in 3 columns + side panel (shop, reputation, log)\n\nAccessibility (NFR-03)\n- Every action is a real <button>, with a visible focus ring\n- Tab order follows the visual order\n- The live log is an aria-live='polite' region\n- The suspense and reveal play in a modal dialog.\n  The result is announced with\n  aria-live='assertive'\n- Contrast is at least 4.5:1 and the risk badges have text\n",
      "originalText": "1  Stats stay visible at all times: lives, gold, level, score,\n   turn (WEB-03). Both screens add the stored high score,\n   raised by games and runs (WEB-18). Lives turn red at 1.\n2  Quest board: ads keep the game's order. The player can sort\n   by reward, expiry or risk. No bot pick, no EV by default (FUN-01).\n   Risk badges are colored and labeled, so color is never the\n   only signal (NFR-03). Encrypted ads appear decoded, with a tag.\n3  Every quest has the same Solve button. Risk shows through the\n   label and 'At stake: 1 life'. Trap tags only appear with the\n   advisor on (WEB-07).\n4  Shop: items the user can't afford are disabled, with a tooltip\n   showing the missing gold (WEB-04).\n   Potion first, because it's the most common purchase.\n5  Event log: newest first. Green = success, red = failure or\n   lost life, blue = purchase (WEB-05).\n6  Run form: validated inline (VAL-04). Stop is enabled only\n   while the selected run is running (WEB-08, BOT-12).\n7  Run list: status badges (running / finished / stopped /\n   failed). Clicking a run opens its live view and history.\n8  Score chart: a dashed 1000 target line shows progress toward\n   the goal at a glance (WEB-09).\n9  Live events stream over SSE with a 'live' dot. The log\n   auto-scrolls unless the user has scrolled up.\n10 Mobile: one column, with stats in a 3x2 grid. Shop, reputation and\n   log open as bottom sheets, with a bottom tab bar for navigation (NFR-01).\n11 Choose: Solve sends the API call at once and locks the other Solve\n   buttons (status: resolving). Shop, Refresh and Investigate stay\n   enabled and queue (WEB-12). Nothing is chosen for the player.\n12 Suspense, in a dialog over the board: the stakes\n   (win gold / lose a life), the risk label and an animation. Hold the result for a minimum time\n   even if the API answers first (FUN-02, FUN-03).\n13 Climax: the copy changes, the progress bar fills, and tension\n   grows with risk (FUN-05).\n14 Reveal, in the same dialog after the suspense phase.\n   Clearly different success and failure, with the game's message\n   and deltas. The stats animate. The result stays until the player\n   presses Continue or Close, then the board is back (FUN-04). Failure on the last\n   life suggests a potion.\n15 Advisor (opt-in): EV and trap tags, but never reorders the\n   board or marks a best pick (WEB-07). EV = p x reward -\n   (1 - p) x lifeCost, lifeCost = 240 / lives (CORE-06).\n   Calculation shown below the advisor sketch.\n16 Milestones: 1000 points, new high score, last life (FUN-08).\n17 Reputation: people, state and underworld, shown with a sign.\n   Unknown until the player presses Investigate, which uses one\n   turn, so it is never automatic. A new game clears it (WEB-16).\n\nResponsive breakpoints\n- < 640px: one column, bottom tabs, sheets\n- 640-1023px: ad grid with 2 columns; shop, reputation and log below\n- >= 1024px: ads in 3 columns + side panel (shop, reputation, log)\n\nAccessibility (NFR-03)\n- Every action is a real <button>, with a visible focus ring\n- Tab order follows the visual order\n- The live log is an aria-live='polite' region\n- The suspense and reveal play in a modal dialog.\n  The result is announced with\n  aria-live='assertive'\n- Contrast is at least 4.5:1 and the risk badges have text\n",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": null,
